# ga-usb-port-allowlist — USB port paths (the sysfs device name) authorized on
# this board, one per line. With usbcore.authorized_default=0 (set in
# uboot-boot.ush) a device binds to a driver only if /usr/libexec/ga-usb-authorize
# finds it here or in /usr/share/ga-usb-allowlist (VID:PID).
#
# These are the board's internal devices behind the on-board hub. A port path
# is fixed by the board wiring: plugging an adapter into an external port can
# not give it one of these names, whatever IDs the adapter reports. External
# ports stay closed; an external device needs a VID:PID declaration.
#
#   3-1     the on-board hub
#   3-1.1   the cellular modem
#   3-1.2   on-board serial radio
#   3-1.3   on-board serial radio
3-1
3-1.1
3-1.2
3-1.3
